<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Na Zangina</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">early 18th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Na Zangina was ya-na (king) of Dagbon in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a> in the early 18th century and is remembered as the first king to adopt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> at court. His reign strengthened ties with Muslim traders and scholars who linked Dagbon to the kola routes between Hausaland and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akan">Akan</a> forest. Islam then became part of royal ritual and administration in the kingdom.</p></div>
